    "final_message": "I wrote the composition, rendered the `story-drafting` tree, wrote both acceptance tests, and committed on the branch. `scripts/verify story-drafting` passes tessercheck (zero findings), `mypy --strict` and every non-root test tier, then fails in the root tier.\n\n- **`tests/test_reading_jtbds.py::TestReadingJtbds::test_s_2_a_1` fails at its *then*.** The host answers 200, but with the stub's placeholder status: `AssertionError: assert 'drafting_stories' == 'awaiting_story_acceptance'`. It asserts that status, at least one story, and that each story has a given, when, then and state \"drafted\".\n- **`tests/test_submitting_jtbds.py::TestSubmittingJtbds::test_s_1_a_1` passes.** Its *then* is a `jtbd_id` and status \"drafting_stories\", and the stubs already satisfy that because an enum read answers its first member and `drafting_stories` is listed first. I left it as written rather than distort it.\n\nComposition:\n- **Aggregate:** `Jtbd`, with the command `record_stories`.\n- **Client operations:** `submit_jtbd` (`POST /jtbds`) and `get_jtbd` (`GET /jtbds/{jtbd_id}`).\n- **Orchestrator:** `conduct_story_drafting`, which runs `story.draft_stories`, then `jtbd.record_stories`, then waits on the signal `accept_stories`.\n- **Ports:** `StoryDrafter` (an agent-owned `TemplateStoryDrafter`), `JtbdRepository` (memory) and `JtbdIdentityRepository` (uuid).\n\nThe decisions I was least sure of:\n- **Signal payload:** `accept_stories` carries only `jtbd_id`. The accepted story set isn't modeled, since accepting is out of scope.\n- **Enum order:** `drafting_stories` comes first in `JtbdStatus`, which is why the submit test already passes.\n- **Action key:** `story` (class `StoryActions`) on port `StoryDrafter`, because the composition rules refuse a key like `drafter`.\n\nThe specs are in `story-drafting/specs/` under `<repo>/`. The commit is `6dd5c46`."
  },
